<PolicyLayout
  title="Contact | Miami Debt Help"
  description="How to reach Miami Debt Help — corrections, listing requests, and general questions."
  lang="en"
  altLangPath="/es/contact/"
  breadcrumbLabel="Contact"
  h1="Contact"
  intro="We're setting up a dedicated contact inbox — check back soon for a direct email address. In the meantime, here's the fastest way to reach us depending on what you need."
>
  <h2>Found something wrong on the site</h2>
  <p>
    Use <a href="/report-an-error/">Report an Error</a> — it routes directly to editorial review
    and is faster than a general message.
  </p>

  <h2>Want your organization listed</h2>
  <p>
    Use <a href="/submit-a-listing/">List Your Organization</a>. Free and paid placements both go
    through the same verification process — see <a href="/how-we-verify/">How We Verify</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Press or media inquiries</h2>
  <p>
    A direct press contact is coming soon along with the general inbox above. If you're a
    journalist working on a Miami-Dade debt or consumer-protection story in the meantime, the
    <a href="/how-we-verify/">How We Verify</a> and <a href="/about/">About</a> pages cover our
    methodology and who's behind the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Everything else</h2>
  <p>
    General questions about the site, its data, or its editorial policy — check
    <a href="/about/">About</a>, <a href="/editorial-independence/">Editorial Independence</a>,
    and <a href="/how-we-make-money/">How We Make Money</a> first; most questions are answered
    there. A direct contact channel for anything not covered is on the way.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
